  left-out: "Three headings in the source carry no prose of their own — History,
    Geography and Economy exist only to introduce their subsections — so their
    bodies are empty rather than filled with invented continuity. The climate
    table, the religion table, the list of titular archbishops, the notable
    people, the popular-culture entries and the twin towns are lists and
    tables, not prose, and are carried across as they stood. Two things in the
    document contradict each other and I have not tried to reconcile them: the
    lead says Baalbek's history dates back at least 11,000 years while the
    Prehistory section says the hilltop shows almost continual habitation over
    the last 8–9000 years, and the article's twin-town list (Bari, L'Aquila,
    Bergama, Thrace, Yogyakarta, Qazvin) does not match the Wikidata claim
    (Qom, Bari, L'Aquila, Yogyakarta, Isfahan, Bergama) — the article's own
    list is what the section reproduces. In the Ruins section the source
    states twice, in consecutive sentences, that the 1759 earthquakes damaged
    the area around the eagle inscription; the rewrite says it once, carrying
    [[ ^109 ]]. The infobox area (7 km2 city, 16 km2 metro) and the Wikidata
    area (37.420 square kilometre) disagree, so no key fact quotes an area."
